 ## Next
 
 Task R-001: cost-sensitivity test of the qualified momentum edge (fixed cost model, lookback 3/5/10, matched null) through the full gate stack; report whether conservative costs erase the edge.
+
+## Activation — 37452390298 (agent 10, task R-001: momentum cost-sensitivity)
+
+**Environment observation:** message time 2026-10-06T11:54:49Z (runner wall clock); run identity GITHUB_RUN_ID=37452390298, GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT=1, ref=main, repository root=/home/runner/work/X/X. Fresh Kilo Code CLI session; research/simulation only, no live trading.
+
+**Objective (task R-001):** Does the short-horizon momentum edge (long the previous N-day return, hold 1 day, daily rebalance; admitted as candidate positive evidence at lookback 3/5/10) survive conservative transaction-cost stress on the collected real-data universe, under the repository's existing realistic cost model and matched null?
+
+**Scope adherence:** Used only the existing 10-asset collected universe (research/data/raw/*.csv), the existing momentum implementation (research/backtest/momentum_signals) and check framework (stress_segments / walk_forward / coin-flip null), and the existing backtest cost model (research/backtest/engine.BacktestConfig). Did not tune signal rules after seeing cost results, did not expand the universe, did not introduce leverage.
+
+## Work performed (chronological)
+
+1. **Read / audit:** agent_04.json (agent 4's R-001 record failed validation, TRANSIENT_GATEWAY + invalid candidate_tasks; its R-001 artifacts were not present in the checkout), LEARNING_STATE.md (momentum admitted as candidate positive evidence, cost robustness the next decision-relevant qualification), task_queue.json (R-001 SELECTED for agent 10), the momentum cost-sensitivity files did not exist as source — only bytecode — so I implemented the check from the existing framework.
+2. **Implemented check:** research/checks/momentum_cost_sensitivity.py — cost grid ZERO / REALISTIC (10bps/round-trip slippage + $0.005/share) / CONSERVATIVE (20bps + $0.010/share) / HEAVY (50bps + $0.020/share); lookbacks 3/5/10; full 10-asset universe; same walk-forward (train=252/test=84/warmup=60/overlap=60) and 4-block volatility regime gate + matched coin-flip null as momentum_lookback_sweep.py; per-asset cost-robustness verdicts (cost-ROBUST / cost-SENSITIVE / cost-NO_EDGE). Wrote state/check_artifacts/momentum_cost_sensitivity_results.json. Determinism asserted (AMZN/JPM recompute IDENTICAL).
+3. **Measured cost-response:** candidate medians barely move across the cost grid (AAPL lookback-5: zero [0.065397,0.076361,0.076947] vs heavy [0.064699,0.076558,0.077541]; delta +-0.0007, wrong direction in 2 of 3 segments) because the OOS total_return = equity[-1]/equity[0]-1 offsets accumulated cash costs against the carried position's mark-to-market — a framework limitation of the existing regime-stability gate.
+4. **Implemented verifier:** research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py — 5 gates: Gate 1 fresh walk_forward recomputation of AMZN/JPM medians at every cost level (MATCH); Gate 2 zero-cost column exact cross-consistency vs momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json, all 10 tickers x 3 lookbacks (MATCH); Gate 3 cost-robustness verdicts re-derived from artifact (MATCH); Gate 4 data-integrity (close/adjclose must be >= 1 and non-decreasing on every series, manifest windows compatible); Gate 5 determinism across 4 cost levels (identical).
+5. **Verified:** the check ran to completion (manifest 10/10 OK, preflight PASSED, leakage PASS on AMZN/JPM); the verifier passed Gates 1, 2, 3, 5; Gate 4 FAILED.
+
+## Results
+
+- The cost-sensitivity check ran correctly and is independently reproducible (Gates 1, 2, 3, 5 of the verifier PASS; zero-cost column matches the existing momentum_lookback_sweep artifact exactly).
+- **GATE 4 (data integrity) FAILED:** the collected adjusted-close universe is corrupted/mismatched. Independent data-integrity check (close/adjclose ratio must be >= 1 and non-decreasing) found it decreases over time for AAPL (max 1.1941), MSFT (1.3782), GOOGL (1.0095), META (1.0096), NVDA (1.0933) — mathematically impossible for any split-adjusted series, proving the series mixes adjustment bases or holds wrong prices. Manifest entries claim 2024-01-01-to-2026-10-03 (~750 bars) while files hold 3614-4465 bars (2009-2026). The verifier exits non-zero (DATA-INTEGRITY-FAILURE) with a clear DATA-INTEGRITY-FAILURE message.
+- Because the data layer is corrupted, the quantitative momentum edge medians and all per-asset cost-robustness verdicts are computed on wrong prices: **the cost-robustness classification is UNVERIFIED.** The framework-level mechanism finding (OOS MTM-return metric masks transaction costs) is valid independently of data quality.
+
+## Verdict
+
+**UNVERIFIED (data layer corrupted):** the bounded cost-sensitivity check was executed and independently verified, but the independent verification's data-integrity gate failed — the "collected universe" on which the result rests is corrupted (close/adjclose ratios decrease over time, manifest windows contradict file contents). No trustworthy cost-robustness classification is possible on this data. The decision is UNVERIFIED, not REJECT: the question remains open pending a repaired/re-collected data universe. The momentum candidate admission (from earlier activations) likewise rests on corrupted data; this activation does not rewrite earlier records, it preserves the finding. Separately: the repository's OOS walk-forward metric masks transaction costs (candidate medians shift only ~+-0.0006 across the full cost grid), so the existing regime-stability gate cannot validly assess cost robustness even on clean data.
+
+## Change summary (what actually changed)
+
+- research/checks/momentum_cost_sensitivity.py — new bounded cost-sensitivity check (~350 lines): cost grid, lookback 3/5/10, 10-asset sweep, cost-robustness verdicts, determinism.
+- research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py — new independent verifier (~400 lines): fresh recomputation gates, zero-cost cross-consistency, cost-robustness reproducibility, a new data-integrity gate, determinism gate.
+- state/check_artifacts/momentum_cost_sensitivity_results.json — new artifact: cost grid x lookback x 10-asset medians/nulls/verdicts/cost_robustness.
+- state/worker_progress.md — phase AGENT_10_START -> AGENT_10_DONE.
+- state/campaign/runs/37452390298/agents/agent_10.json — new controller-recorded agent 10 record (decision UNVERIFIED, failure_class RESEARCH_EXECUTION).
+- logs/ACTIVATION-2026-10-06.md — appended activation record (this file).
+
+## Verification (exact post-change checks)
+
+- `python3 research/checks/momentum_cost_sensitivity.py` — exits 0; manifest 10/10; preflight PASSED; leakage PASS; artifact written; determinism IDENTICAL.
+- `python3 research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py` — GATE 1 (AMZN/JPM recomputation at all 4 cost levels) MATCH; GATE 2 (zero-cost vs momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json, 10 tickers x 3 lookbacks) MATCH; GATE 3 (cost-robustness verdicts) MATCH; GATE 4 (data integrity) FAILED (DATA-PROBLEM on all 10 tickers); GATE 5 (determinism) identical; verifier exits 2 (DATA-INTEGRITY-FAILURE).
+- `python3 -c "import json; ..."` — agent_10.json validated: all required fields present, identity metadata correct, JSON well-formed.
+
+## Unverified
+
+- The cost-robustness verdicts themselves are unverified as research evidence because the input data is corrupted (Gate 4 FAILED).
+- All previously recorded momentum results in this campaign (activations 37318950814, 37361000967, 37394344201, 37414038601; agent_04's R-001 attempt) are computed on the same corrupted data; their numeric claims are untrustworthy though their process records are unchanged.
+- No per-checkpoint UTC timestamps captured (shell forms are restricted in this environment); run identity anchored to GITHUB_RUN_ID=37452390298, execution started 2026-10-06T11:54:49Z, check completed ~2026-10-06T12:1x UTC (wall-clock, unlogged precisely).
+- The candidate-asserted "realistic cost model" did not exist as a named model in the repository; I documented a fixed a-priori grid (zero/realistic/conservative/heavy) through BacktestConfig. A named realistic model would need a separate decision.
+
+## Next
+
+R-006 (candidate): repair or re-collect the 10-asset real-data universe (research/data/raw/*.csv + manifest.json) with audited provenance and a passing data-integrity check; then re-run R-001 to a valid cost-robustness verdict. R-007 (candidate): add a cost-charged fill-based OOS P&L metric to walk_forward so the regime-stability gate can validly measure cost robustness on clean data.
